# Paying Pyrrhic Strike's blight means choosing both modes, and a mode with no legal target can't be chosen (CR 700.2a),
# so with no creature of mana value 3 or greater anywhere (Bot2's Tarmogoyf is mana value 2, Bot1's Ornithopter 0) the
# blight is not on offer, though Bot1 controls a creature to blight. Cast without it, the one mode destroys Bot2's Mox Pearl.
# (pyrrhic-strike-with-blight-paid-chooses-both-modes is the same cast with both modes open, where the blight is offered.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Pyrrhic Strike
Plains x3
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Tarmogoyf
Island x4
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Tarmogoyf.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pyrrhic Strike.Cast
! Bot1.Modes(Blight 2)
Bot1.Modes(Cast without blighting)
Bot1.Modes(1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Sol Ring; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.MinusOneMinusOne = (absent)
Bot2.Graveyard = Mox Pearl
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Tarmogoyf
